      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a fragment shader, FragCoord doesn\u0027t need special treatment; it exists in the module as a variable with a builtin layout value:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/sksl_frag.sksl;l\u003d4;drc\u003dd3ecfb3bb86a62fa0643a7dda24701b8e1ef4d00\n\nWe already had a test for sk_FragCoord here:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:resources/sksl/shared/FragCoords.sksl;drc\u003d82915f80e341bea2b122d0a2cdd05aee3b51ff93\n\nHowever, this test was previously written in \"runtime effect\" style (returns half4, takes float2) so it wasn\u0027t really a good test. I\u0027ve reworked it in this CL to use a \"fragment\" style (returns/takes nothing). This is just a better test all around:\n\nhttps://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/752379/5/resources/sksl/shared/FragCoords.sksl",
